I can see that, it makes a lot of sense, you know?

00:40:24.800 --> 00:40:26.800
And, I mean, in ways, even the,

00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:29.800
I would say the kind of more progressive liberal spirit

00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:32.800
is mostly down for this critique, you know?

00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:34.800
So, for example, the notions of tolerance

00:40:34.800 --> 00:40:36.800
and, you know, a kind of openness.

00:40:36.800 --> 00:40:41.800
Like, yeah, there's something good there.

00:40:41.800 --> 00:40:42.800
Or even a kind of openness like, hey,

00:40:42.800 --> 00:40:44.800
okay, so we take this capital T truth

00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:48.800
that's kind of been chopped down to lowercase t truths.

00:40:48.800 --> 00:40:53.800
So, now it's sort of like, well, there's just truths.

00:40:53.800 --> 00:40:54.800
You know what I mean?

00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:55.800
Just truths, and not the truth,

00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:57.800
like this is the truth, you better believe it, you know,

00:40:57.800 --> 00:40:59.800
but it's just truths, you have your truth,

00:40:59.800 --> 00:41:00.800
and I have my truth, and we're, you know,

00:41:00.800 --> 00:41:03.800
we're kind of doing our best here.

00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:08.800
So, what's the kind of challenge to this?

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:10.800
Well, this leads to what Alistair MacIntyre,

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:13.800
he calls it emotivism.

00:41:13.800 --> 00:41:15.800
The view that moral judgments are mere expressions

00:41:15.800 --> 00:41:17.800
of approval or disapproval,

00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:20.800
not whether they are true or false.

00:41:20.800 --> 00:41:22.800
This would be the challenge, like,

00:41:22.800 --> 00:41:23.800
if you're kind of like, yeah,

00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:25.800
I'm done with that other view of truth,

00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:26.800
you know, now I'm just embracing this one.

00:41:27.800 --> 00:41:29.800
This would be the kind of Achilles heel

00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:31.800
of this perspective, right?

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:32.800
Because this goes fine,

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:33.800
especially for stuff that doesn't really matter,

00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:35.800
like, oh, you have your opinions, I have mine, whatever,

00:41:35.800 --> 00:41:36.800
you know, live and let live, it's cool.

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:38.800
But until we bump up against things where it's like,

00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:40.800
oh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no,

00:41:40.800 --> 00:41:42.800
well, this really matters.

00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:44.800
This is a belief.

00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:47.800
This is a story or whatever,

00:41:47.800 --> 00:41:49.800
like, I think this really matters,

00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:52.800
and suddenly we're having conflict with one another.

00:41:52.800 --> 00:41:53.800
It could be across cultures,

00:41:53.800 --> 00:41:55.800
or it could be even, you know, within a culture,

00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:57.800
within a church, you know.

00:41:57.800 --> 00:41:58.800
Even, like, the broader church,

00:41:58.800 --> 00:42:01.800
